  [34mexport[39m [34mconst[39m [33mrequired[39m  = (msg = [31m"This field is required"[39m) => [33m([39mv) => v.[33mtrim[39m() ? [34mnull[39m : msg;
  [34mexport[39m [34mconst[39m [33mminLength[39m = (n, msg) => [33m([39mv) => v.length >= n ? [34mnull[39m : msg ?? [31m`Must be at least [39m${n} characters`;
  [34mexport[39m [34mconst[39m [33mpattern[39m   = (re, msg) => [33m([39mv) => re.[33mtest[39m(v) ? [34mnull[39m : msg;

  Three validators is the whole starter set — [38;5;153mpattern[39m covers email and the rest until a real form asks for more.

  [1mThe core is one pure function:[0m

  [34mexport[39m [34mfunction[39m [33mvalidate[39m(values, schema) → { valid, errors }
  [32m// schema: { username: [required()], password: [required(), minLength(8)] }[39m
  [32m// errors: { username: "This field is required" }   // first failing rule per field wins[39m

  [1mThe binder is thin and dumb:[0m

  [34mexport[39m [34mfunction[39m [33mbindForm[39m(formEl, schema, onValid)

  On submit it calls [38;5;153mpreventDefault()[39m, collects values from [38;5;153m[name][39m inputs, runs [38;5;153mvalidate[39m, writes each message into
  [38;5;153m[data-error-for="<name>"][39m (clearing stale ones), and calls [38;5;153monValid(values)[39m only if clean. Two conventions total — [38;5;153mname
[39m  attributes and the error spans — so swapping the binder out costs nothing if form #2 disagrees.

  [1mConsequences worth your yes before I start:[0m [38;5;153mvalidateForm()[39m in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m gets deleted, and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m changes — inputs
  gain [38;5;153mname[39m, error [38;5;153m<span>[39ms get added, [38;5;153m<script>[39m becomes [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m. User-visible behavior changes too, for the better:
  today a failed login logs [38;5;153m"Missing required fields"[39m to the console and shows the user nothing; after this, each field
  shows its own message on the page. The page will need to be served over HTTP rather than opened as a file.

  Alongside that, the tooling question — this repo has none configured, and it's cheapest to add now:
